# Node32-HUB — Third-Party Notices

This firmware statically links third-party libraries under open-source
licenses. Those libraries remain under their own licenses; the MIT notice in
`LICENSE` applies only to first-party code.

Compliance materials (sources + relinkable objects for the LGPL libraries and
all license texts) are generated on demand by
`chatgpt/scripts/package_third_party.py` into `chatgpt/build/third-party/` (staging area).
`chatgpt/rename_firmware.py` refreshes it per board and packs it as
`third-party.zip` inside every per-build output folder, so each build
folder can be shared or sold as-is. `chatgpt/rename_firmware.py` copies that bundle — together with
`LICENSE`, `THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES` and `SBOM.md` — into every per-build output
folder (`chatgpt/build/<board>/<pack>/<version>/<timestamp>/`), so each build
folder can be shared or sold as-is.

