## 1. LGPL libraries (statically linked — compliance materials required)

In accordance with the LGPL, the source code of these libraries is provided
unchanged, together with relinkable objects, so that you may modify and
relink them.

### LGPL-3.0-only

| Library | Version | Upstream | Compliance materials |
|---|---|---|---|
| ESP32Async/AsyncTCP | 3.5.0 | https://github.com/ESP32Async/AsyncTCP | `chatgpt/build/third-party/lgpl-sources/AsyncTCP/`, `chatgpt/build/third-party/lgpl-objects/<env>/AsyncTCP/` |
| ESP32Async/ESPAsyncWebServer | 3.12.1 | https://github.com/ESP32Async/ESPAsyncWebServer | `chatgpt/build/third-party/lgpl-sources/ESPAsyncWebServer/`, `chatgpt/build/third-party/lgpl-objects/<env>/ESPAsyncWebServer/` |
| rlogiacco/CircularBuffer | 1.4.0 | https://github.com/rlogiacco/CircularBuffer | `chatgpt/build/third-party/lgpl-sources/CircularBuffer/`, `chatgpt/build/third-party/lgpl-objects/<env>/CircularBuffer/` |

`<env>` is the PlatformIO environment the objects were compiled for
(`n16r8`, `waveshare_8di8do`, `esp32p4`, …). Ship the objects for every board
you distribute, since architectures differ (S3 xtensa vs P4 RISC-V).

### LGPL-2.1-only

| Library | Version | Upstream | Compliance materials |
|---|---|---|---|
| arduino-esp32 core (framework) | 3.3.5 | https://github.com/espressif/arduino-esp32 | `chatgpt/build/third-party/lgpl-sources/arduino-esp32/` |

> The arduino-esp32 core is provided by the PlatformIO toolchain
> (`~/.platformio/packages/framework-arduinoespressif32`). Its source is
> bundled unchanged in `chatgpt/build/third-party/lgpl-sources/arduino-esp32/` by the
> packaging script.

License texts: `chatgpt/build/third-party/licences/LGPL-2.1.txt`, `chatgpt/build/third-party/licences/LGPL-3.0.txt`.

